#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059771 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059580 :question/id #uuid "836f2f1b-5dd4-5dba-81cc-eb9ffe7db8d1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4693" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n![](images/62/627d12115d61ddfdedf9db08330269de2137a23abceada977d039e90e5b88675.png)\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation $R_2 := R_2 +(- 4) \\cdot R_1$ on $A?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation $R_2:=R_2 + (-4) R_1$ means that we need to add $-4$ times the first row to the second row. \n\nCarrying out this row operation, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 12 & 13\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-4)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4+(-4)(1) & 2+(-4)(2) & -1+(-4)(3) \\\\ 7 & 12 & 13\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -13 \\\\ 7 & 12 & 13\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb1afe82-86ba-5a15-9037-74717692ecb2" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050163 :topic/math-academy-id 1167 :topic/title "Index Notation for Matrices"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059961 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5a9bba7-f581-5372-a873-0fc17a55fb02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & -9 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056126} {:answer/id #uuid "b9c177a1-6771-55e3-bd09-bf47def49ac2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 & 9 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056127} {:answer/id #uuid "0d1d8e7e-44fc-5700-9bdc-f19ade4437e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056128} {:answer/id #uuid "5f95897b-76c9-50f9-ba67-9a60ae42a4ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056129} {:answer/id #uuid "64489d72-05e0-5199-9ab5-2517bee16eda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056130}] :answer-field/id #uuid "fe11ff0e-55ca-57c1-896c-442215af5968" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056125} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e95e2e5-f4c7-556f-9d3b-6806aa203aac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386022} {:answer/id #uuid "93d2127b-e5d6-5f6a-b77b-e49e6b3917a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386023} {:answer/id #uuid "dfcd1624-4c95-5d1d-b7c3-eadfb5affb1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & -9 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386024} {:answer/id #uuid "84d65aa0-7f3f-56d8-8813-60439890bf5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386025} {:answer/id #uuid "f47ccd2f-8569-5e0e-ae2f-f78a4ee09a4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 & 9 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e95e2e5-f4c7-556f-9d3b-6806aa203aac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386022} :answer-field/id #uuid "6265e561-15e0-5e23-846a-8eab1f2ab8dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386021}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "73199f2e-4821-5c88-b3d1-fc53d8677008" :question/math-academy-id "q-10248" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $M,$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1}$ on $M?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $3$ times the first row to the third row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3+(3)(-1) & -1+(3)(2) & 9+(3)(4)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 21\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059962 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03dc59cb-fd09-565f-9b4f-7c5b09fa0d6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235821} {:answer/id #uuid "13851fd1-8586-537b-b24a-6845ca174846" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235931} {:answer/id #uuid "2ca00ef3-9d64-5399-b711-41bbe0eaeaea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236097} {:answer/id #uuid "7c169d8a-0156-5a46-bcad-6fcf3b499bde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236593} {:answer/id #uuid "c6f87e96-eee1-5c3b-b11d-b31db823cd13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c169d8a-0156-5a46-bcad-6fcf3b499bde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236593} :answer-field/id #uuid "1923a0a4-f52b-5133-bedc-c31b8ed88e76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237468}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "855eebc5-e47a-5262-b735-bfa0d3ece889" :question/math-academy-id "q-10250" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ on $A?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ means that we need to swap the first and second rows.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237897 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b0ae7c7-831d-5433-9390-889330306d24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235871} {:answer/id #uuid "30eaaa83-5cd1-5e22-a46e-6e3b5195a079" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236128} {:answer/id #uuid "bab3efd1-d5b4-58ad-bfff-d99746961975" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237011} {:answer/id #uuid "df090ab6-463d-55fd-9c82-27652ad50d03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237219} {:answer/id #uuid "faa1874f-baa6-5eb3-8044-094998eb5d5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237402}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df090ab6-463d-55fd-9c82-27652ad50d03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237219} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d143e11-fa10-5879-b30c-3e557bb06f36" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237518}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "89449fa7-e2ad-5aa8-8f8e-c30702d39ac6" :question/math-academy-id "q-10244" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ on $A?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}$ means that we need to swap the first and second rows.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265796 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0afbf473-cf2c-557a-b166-cf94f46b04fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{7}{3} \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 9 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263105} {:answer/id #uuid "39cae253-d68f-537c-b71f-b07e5c03621e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ \\frac{7}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 1 \\\\ 6 & 9 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263515} {:answer/id #uuid "5c917f32-40fe-536b-976e-64ddba176487" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263800} {:answer/id #uuid "d2202449-4412-5126-800a-2b62df1d2a71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264833} {:answer/id #uuid "fc2ff622-6bf9-5fc1-9910-0b357c357bf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 18 & 27 & -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2202449-4412-5126-800a-2b62df1d2a71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264833} :answer-field/id #uuid "a68b5eeb-7e97-5637-b883-d5b1091e0338" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265542}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1b5f24a7-25be-5f91-9261-490e6919b435" :question/math-academy-id "q-130006" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 9 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}$ on $A?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3}$ means that we need to multiply the third row of the matrix by $\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nMultiplying the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{3}$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 9 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:=\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 6 & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 9 & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265809 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73a2c4e4-50d2-503f-bd6c-ff089298616e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264003} {:answer/id #uuid "7ff361c5-1ff3-5bae-bd7f-64bc0ff75321" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 8 & -9 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264101} {:answer/id #uuid "a4eeb7c2-1749-5db5-9f69-4de6d50bbc49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264408} {:answer/id #uuid "a8f82394-8f99-5fa4-ba5d-107b492af231" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264445} {:answer/id #uuid "bacc0ddd-dc83-59e3-9874-8cfac2adf105" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264622}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4eeb7c2-1749-5db5-9f69-4de6d50bbc49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264408} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ed109b8-a919-5012-a65d-4a4d80d99f80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265361}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "89540d9f-9bfa-5f07-91be-e72783b1a7bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-130064" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $C,$ given by\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $C?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2}$ means that we need to add $-2$ times the second row to the first row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{2}$ means that we need to add $1$ times the second row to the third row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-2)\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0+(-2)(5) & 4+(-2)(2) & 7+(-2)(1) \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(1)\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1+(1)(5) & 3+(1)(2) & 0+(1)(1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265810 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03949c4b-6891-5b84-b41d-57552e4e94cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263030} {:answer/id #uuid "5841ddf4-5f71-5cdd-afc7-47cedd7a87e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -19 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263760} {:answer/id #uuid "aaef4050-007d-5267-8d48-c8df487afab0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264465} {:answer/id #uuid "be5ea1db-c697-51d4-aeb0-b74aead3cc03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264654} {:answer/id #uuid "c8d8bd0a-43ee-511e-985d-7a0790baba7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -9 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264760}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03949c4b-6891-5b84-b41d-57552e4e94cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263030} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d7835eb-fe41-51f2-8257-6d4458713548" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265496}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "873c8162-c75c-5ddc-aed6-146d6160fb0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-130065" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $C,$ given by\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $C?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+3{R}_{3} \\\\ {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $3$ times the third row to the first row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $5$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1+(3)(2) & 2+(3)(0) & 1+(3)(-1) \\\\ -9 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -9 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -9+(5)(2) & 0+(5)(0) & -4+(5)(-1) \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287981 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f838c2c-b1d0-52ca-bdd1-759b3f28e9b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285663} {:answer/id #uuid "6d2a787c-8b97-57cc-8fe2-47181a3b7d2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285790} {:answer/id #uuid "77cd75e4-8855-5c13-9dee-73fe9f426575" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -7 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285902} {:answer/id #uuid "b0405152-868b-5aca-9457-e8ef9b46e55b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286397} {:answer/id #uuid "f1bcca47-aebf-5c20-bf86-bec34ef21f8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -10 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f838c2c-b1d0-52ca-bdd1-759b3f28e9b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285663} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6cd03db-7e93-5314-902f-ae586cc7310d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287587}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e33508b0-e7bc-5f7b-ba8e-f8058d2dcab4" :question/math-academy-id "q-20239" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1}$ on $X?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $-3$ times the first row to the second row. \n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3)\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3+(-3)(1) & -1+(-3)(2) & 1+(-3)(1) \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -7 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386014 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17d6b6ba-73af-5b0e-aadb-df2b92946446" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386016} {:answer/id #uuid "fd96430f-7419-56b6-99da-8a526bba22e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 21 & 27 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386017} {:answer/id #uuid "83bf736c-a7af-587e-9671-a0755c99d45c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386018} {:answer/id #uuid "be7cd770-89d2-5f9f-b60e-e8df5d9ff51c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386019} {:answer/id #uuid "f19e8491-c92c-5661-8c92-a31904c65e32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 25 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83bf736c-a7af-587e-9671-a0755c99d45c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386018} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f488fbc-4f0a-58a9-aca2-89c02a7e41b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386015}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d89fad28-1b46-55f3-b90e-6ed4c3f194da" :question/math-academy-id "q-10245" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 12 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $B?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $4$ times the first row to the second row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $1$ times the first row to the third row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -4 & 12 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ -4+(4)(1) & 12+(4)(3) & 3+(4)(6) \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ -1+1 & 2+3 & 4+6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 24 & 27 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 10\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388062 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3918bbf4-16cc-5c1f-a802-36adb86390c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ -14 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388064} {:answer/id #uuid "e62342b5-074d-5e24-9642-83584f678838" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 30 & 11 & -20 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388065} {:answer/id #uuid "b6849f47-5bf1-537e-9558-fee095da4647" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 28 & 15 & -23 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388066} {:answer/id #uuid "7c6fc884-3dee-5e5f-9162-e9d9a9e34a9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ -5 & 9 & -11 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388067} {:answer/id #uuid "22917917-c3d7-5ada-b4ca-d45cebf96675" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 26 & 19 & -26 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e62342b5-074d-5e24-9642-83584f678838" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 30 & 11 & -20 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388065} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9ef02a3-2e92-5a2e-a56c-df3ea22f0bc2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388063}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d1a5db75-1b21-5cae-946a-8cdf4a8b6bd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-130010" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $C,$ given by\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $C?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $3$ times the first row to the second row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3\\cdot {R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 1+(3)(9) & -3+(3)(6) & -2+(3)(-7) \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 28 & 15 & -23 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1)\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 28+(-1)(-2) & 15+(-1)(4) & -23+(-1)(-3) \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 & -7 \\\\ 30 & 11 & -20 \\\\ -2 & 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations To a Coefficients Matrix"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129113 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128925 :question/id #uuid "674e7733-7a8e-5804-a867-82c74c583dcc" :question/math-academy-id "e-4687" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n![](images/27/2701e789f5d3f6fc48fda87706add41ccb59c92d5bae4a76e84ac1abfdce6f07.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The first matrix is not in row echelon form since $a_{32} \\neq 0$ (condition II is violated).\n![](images/d8/d8725937a4f5f1cfcd36cbe4871a872187df071b54c15d2e29d9b1e3c5f9b731.svg)\n\n- The second matrix is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n![](images/5e/5e3142b1ad4bb219db5d5b144e47fe8d1fa8d1f92c300c6f60fc145cf9424900.svg)\n\n- The third matrix is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n![](images/93/9331fdbede7da49e2dbbc66aac0b3084b1c7acca1ac7e789eded304956a18500.svg)\n\n- The fourth matrix is not in row echelon form since, for example, the leading entry $a_{22}$ lies to the left of the leading entry $a_{13}$ (condition II is violated).\n![](images/76/76e7add6349e0b2fceddf094ac6e3e8cfd0bf1bb43a3fbee0c143b256b81f1c5.svg)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050765 :topic/math-academy-id 148 :topic/title "Systems of Equations as Augmented Matrices"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129771 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6ac301d-037b-5334-b6d2-fec88197d154" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459951} {:answer/id #uuid "5d1e6f74-c495-5ab5-805c-d983bca1e55c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459952}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d1e6f74-c495-5ab5-805c-d983bca1e55c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459952} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d0e98e1-9e1f-510d-9dad-15a86b32835a" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460842} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b9aa059-0eae-5a76-81c6-21892541d8ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459953} {:answer/id #uuid "0816847a-d539-509b-8356-6a24a780f633" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459954}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0816847a-d539-509b-8356-6a24a780f633" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459954} :answer-field/id #uuid "5488b353-c1b4-5e30-83ca-a801084429aa" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460843} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd314e1a-8262-5acc-90db-8b8b4a9f82f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459955} {:answer/id #uuid "69a17d39-0448-5a32-8559-ff5820bddc16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459956}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd314e1a-8262-5acc-90db-8b8b4a9f82f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459955} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb9e86fc-fb03-5653-aa77-b599aca20dc9" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460844}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "658776f4-d49a-5e5d-a10c-50a3db34ad1c" :question/math-academy-id "q-42006" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 3 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 5\\end{array}\\right],\\,B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right],\\,C=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 3 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since ${c}_{22}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129774 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a12a5bf1-b831-57bc-a289-9b874dd28be1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128126} {:answer/id #uuid "0e2e8497-890f-5946-abdd-026c91a6a710" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128127} {:answer/id #uuid "3dd70ee5-9437-5935-856c-7e5b9161b173" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128128} {:answer/id #uuid "4e86f997-55ba-53d9-bd8d-f236034d4a69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128129} {:answer/id #uuid "760682b7-9922-52d7-815c-3ae2e12e96e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128130}] :answer-field/id #uuid "84381930-6037-567a-be17-89c5aa7ee6ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128125}] :question/id #uuid "532660a0-b7ef-5857-a687-9a224039f8a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-42026" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n$A = \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 3\\end{array}\\right], B = \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 6\\end{array}\\right], C = \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & 0 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262994 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50c7f862-fb53-52f3-a851-3a1c0dd668c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463742} {:answer/id #uuid "9091f23b-5dc1-5b2b-9de6-80e0b5f2b4c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9091f23b-5dc1-5b2b-9de6-80e0b5f2b4c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463743} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fe6ae55-4a0c-5261-a839-a0dc70994f94" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464805} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0925c8c8-8cf1-5109-b122-e948506d2229" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463744} {:answer/id #uuid "87fde758-761e-5f44-8ba8-4f420469834a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463745}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87fde758-761e-5f44-8ba8-4f420469834a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463745} :answer-field/id #uuid "55a0a25b-6999-500b-b7c6-387f861bd084" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464806} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef038684-e790-5680-b0cf-14a5f0791fb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463746} {:answer/id #uuid "8b0db024-6fc1-5cf1-b6bd-6a6d4a68ed1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463747}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b0db024-6fc1-5cf1-b6bd-6a6d4a68ed1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463747} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8f73348-51d4-578b-b6eb-9e0e603a1638" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464807}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b5479435-9835-502a-bd24-1f955706f0c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-129228" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right],\\,B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 7 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right],\\,C=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 9 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 7 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 9 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ are in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262996 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6490d7cb-e49e-5df3-bd24-1fb08e93c1c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463748} {:answer/id #uuid "73f708ba-0076-5c0b-82e1-e919017f5605" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463749}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73f708ba-0076-5c0b-82e1-e919017f5605" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463749} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ffde19d-784a-502b-8888-25092d71c5ef" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464808} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4750390-d10c-5792-9210-4b235f6e2ce3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463750} {:answer/id #uuid "12e6cef5-b5fe-562c-99cb-370bb6c94767" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463751}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12e6cef5-b5fe-562c-99cb-370bb6c94767" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463751} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a6c5020-e558-5ac4-9259-bee888bb6216" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464809} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88129b53-c2d6-50ae-872d-5f80d5c513e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463752} {:answer/id #uuid "8783247a-7590-53f9-8739-7072f4b6b889" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463753}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8783247a-7590-53f9-8739-7072f4b6b889" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463753} :answer-field/id #uuid "90f5dc9c-b2f5-5481-a853-5afc90c32ea7" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464810}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0ce5c5ca-b382-5ac8-8df3-b2e87f07de7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-129232" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 7\\end{array}\\right],\\,B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-6 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right],\\,C=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}0 & 1 & -4 & 5 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\nI. All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\nII. Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{33}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 7\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since the third row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-6 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since ${c}_{33}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}0 & 1 & -4 & 5 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ are **not** in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262997 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2be017f-5e49-5ecf-9256-9026e1e49309" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463754} {:answer/id #uuid "64657d11-388e-5eea-8953-1183ad80b2a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64657d11-388e-5eea-8953-1183ad80b2a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463755} :answer-field/id #uuid "7df1ad99-8fc0-5931-8c43-c2f5f1f4ae55" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464811} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "183285c5-ecf3-5b1b-a709-43802b2d5542" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463756} {:answer/id #uuid "d06d9b80-8f1e-5a1e-92a5-1af63957f4d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "183285c5-ecf3-5b1b-a709-43802b2d5542" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463756} :answer-field/id #uuid "42b05519-bc6b-5846-bb0a-d39f6aaa1a8f" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464812} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b18bdf6-939a-51c6-93bc-947f0d9b20e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463758} {:answer/id #uuid "a14bc920-ef18-5bb6-a154-ff32ab552a62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b18bdf6-939a-51c6-93bc-947f0d9b20e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463758} :answer-field/id #uuid "92ef8c8f-928a-51da-a3d5-e1b9fb740fb3" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464813}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "842b19e0-4a35-57fa-95ff-d59ed695ed85" :question/math-academy-id "q-129233" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 6\\end{array}\\right],\\,B=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}9 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right],\\,C=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the first row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 6\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}9 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ is **not** in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326923 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82ceb6ee-967f-51f6-9562-a946e9616bd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467488} {:answer/id #uuid "5a978d2b-7bde-5c45-a243-0e4e0a33fde7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82ceb6ee-967f-51f6-9562-a946e9616bd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467488} :answer-field/id #uuid "f80dcb05-a2c2-516d-80fe-1ab0eed4e12b" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468465} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b08f801-3599-510d-8753-6582f23b7efe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467490} {:answer/id #uuid "62d0a2f4-51a8-5771-9041-0b5950520f2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b08f801-3599-510d-8753-6582f23b7efe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467490} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d4a18d9-f146-57c1-98ce-7671782922ed" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468466} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7ed2b63-95a4-56b7-afb2-010d21ef08ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467492} {:answer/id #uuid "158e4809-5e64-50a5-af3e-ca976103a4d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467493}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "158e4809-5e64-50a5-af3e-ca976103a4d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467493} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bbb80cd-ffa5-5028-b638-d29609a12eae" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468467}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "324c0e93-0bc4-5958-ba8a-b87ad1b81b6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-42028" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices have coefficient matrices in row echelon form? Treat the final column of each augmented matrix as its constants column.\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 4\\end{array}\\right],\\,\\,B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 11\\end{array}\\right],\\,\\,C=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 4 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{32}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since the first row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 11\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 4 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341835 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7311cb50-f585-5f8b-8c7c-43ea3935ca30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467950} {:answer/id #uuid "5df8e8f3-9308-5944-af31-4d14c71a9d43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7311cb50-f585-5f8b-8c7c-43ea3935ca30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467950} :answer-field/id #uuid "00781771-aeb9-5835-884e-fa3c06c40e7e" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468696} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1ee2b9e-ef1d-59cf-bd65-2b7d6a2bf08f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467952} {:answer/id #uuid "d81beee0-f7cd-5ee1-a153-c2609ec12ad8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d81beee0-f7cd-5ee1-a153-c2609ec12ad8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467953} :answer-field/id #uuid "625436a2-9099-57c0-a144-3cefd737c380" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468697} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a341d39f-fed1-52da-a5bf-5551842652b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467954} {:answer/id #uuid "5061ada4-2851-5b12-9dcc-a52396a7b645" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467955}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5061ada4-2851-5b12-9dcc-a52396a7b645" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467955} :answer-field/id #uuid "4691ceca-21a9-5d3f-be55-1f587cc36770" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468698}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4f7d9000-6b1e-59bb-84e6-86f972afc228" :question/math-academy-id "q-72570" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 9 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 3\\end{array}\\right],\\,\\,B=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}0 & 2 & 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 11 & 1\\end{array}\\right],\\,\\,C=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}7 & 6 & 6 & 8 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 6\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 9 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$  is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}0 & 2 & 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 11 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}7 & 6 & 6 & 8 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 6\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ and $C$ are in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341837 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "871c0b9a-48a3-59d8-9e1f-f4475d4555bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value 