7f-59fa-9d55-4c82bc621cc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-72574" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices have coefficient matrices in row echelon form? Treat the final column of each augmented matrix as its constants column.\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}6 & 0 & 0 & 8 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right],\\,\\,B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}8 & 7 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 9\\end{array}\\right],\\,\\,C=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied). \n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}6 & 0 & 0 & 8 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}8 & 7 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since ${c}_{21}\\ne 0$ (condition  II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 1 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341838 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60637292-3e09-530b-ac61-fcbbce897d41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467962} {:answer/id #u