"q-72576" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{array}\\right],\\,B=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 0 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right],\\,C=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 0 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & 0 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since ${c}_{21}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 0 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ is in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400436 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c63daf6f-eed4-503b-a8b2-0baf04238897" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472610} {:answer/id #uuid "8c490ab2-ec7b-5dee-94e0-ca23a50fdead" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c490ab2-ec7b-5dee-94e0-ca23a50fdead" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472611} :answer-field/id #uuid "27d756e8-4693-5c8d-a097-a9d17ac33b68" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473700} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "360e1f52-5cdb-5c5e-9a6d-33c968fdb021" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472612} {:answer/id #uuid "cd099e05-d512-5614-a6fc-51d408232f9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472613}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd099e05-d512-5614-a6fc-51d408232f9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472613} :answer-field/id #uuid "3642312c-08a2-5f05-bb3f-1054acc8e9f4" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473701} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e87742a-dcd6-5298-bb30-ef2ace74838c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472614} {:answer/id #uuid "6e8e3db4-35ea-53de-88a3-45ed4615b36f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472615}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e87742a-dcd6-5298-bb30-ef2ace74838c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472614} :answer-field/id #uuid "924222e4-fc3d-551f-a6c3-451ea17542f0" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473702}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3d92198e-4ce7-5520-a0eb-698c6d6eae5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-129231" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right],\\,B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}5 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right],\\,C=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -5 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since ${b}_{33}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}5 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}1 & -5 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are **not** in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405146 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aeca3672-af73-5de4-ae92-8d2b7267905b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473302} {:answer/id #uuid "3762310e-4280-5383-a623-be69110b6dd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aeca3672-af73-5de4-ae92-8d2b7267905b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473302} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b242a5e-e0c2-5c98-9faf-9932a432bab4" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474046} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c468a92d-1de4-54b3-98e3-28167311714f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473304} {:answer/id #uuid "cc55be58-e4c5-5d28-bde2-dd07f224de99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc55be58-e4c5-5d28-bde2-dd07f224de99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473305} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa9139c6-224d-5848-a9fd-c41516bf7428" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474047} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61bba97e-fa99-5844-b1d0-4a1ac0911bd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473306} {:answer/id #uuid "27aa4326-84a9-502a-8ac6-38a05b1d7790" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61bba97e-fa99-5844-b1d0-4a1ac0911bd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473306} :answer-field/id #uuid "17d4295d-6d7f-5bde-a6ed-7e5d41c2a614" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474048}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bbb2727c-01c4-5345-9e38-1d38c7fb43da" :question/math-academy-id "q-72575" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices have coefficient matrices that are **not** in row echelon form? Treat the final column of each augmented matrix as its constants column.\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4\\end{array}\\right],\\,B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 5 & 5\\end{array}\\right],\\,C=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccccc|c}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A coefficient matrix, obtained by omitting the final column of its augmented matrix, is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $B$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entries of its first two rows are in columns $3$ and $2,$ respectively (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 4 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 5 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccccc|c}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ has a coefficient matrix that is **not** in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413825 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ff7ff1b-7d10-5900-8b02-8d8762f4648a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472604} {:answer/id #uuid "2a735909-2afd-58c0-8065-6f9b0fda657e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ff7ff1b-7d10-5900-8b02-8d8762f4648a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472604} :answer-field/id #uuid "f09fe1a5-baa2-5973-acbf-a84cc0ff0a30" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473697} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9738a799-c696-51e8-87a0-1ab427da9e38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472606} {:answer/id #uuid "af5402ff-243c-585f-b25c-a8687187c616" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472607}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af5402ff-243c-585f-b25c-a8687187c616" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472607} :answer-field/id #uuid "1021401d-9baa-5256-9d91-aea06ee1499d" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473698} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b14007f-a781-5311-9863-6ad6959abeb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472608} {:answer/id #uuid "d335439c-9eef-5cb8-852d-d00750680628" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472609}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d335439c-9eef-5cb8-852d-d00750680628" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472609} :answer-field/id #uuid "05c9c089-5c63-5c77-b946-3743f2d68ce2" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473699}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a0f43991-a609-584a-a820-e263b283da38" :question/math-academy-id "q-129230" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}-5 & 0 & 8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{array}\\right],\\,B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & 0 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right],\\,C=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -9 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{33}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}-5 & 0 & 8 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & 0 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -9 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ and $C$ are in row echelon form."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Augmented Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129114 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128926 :question/id #uuid "b6e4983b-c695-5944-9637-6d7547dae849" :question/math-academy-id "e-4688" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n![](images/56/564d16a59313514424d24b8c247d8a3516bfa32188292d2cbc7fee7faf2f5744.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it sa