21-63a0ff1205ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-72492" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\nI. All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\nII. Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry ${c}_{22}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is **not** in row echelon form."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413824 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47c544f2-0094-5efb-b9d7-430a6628b03a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473118} {:answer/id #uuid "d6421a79-149e-5798-8b1f-119bfea53fe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473119}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47c544f2-0094-5efb-b9d7-430a6628b03a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473118} :answer-field/id #uuid "fafc7937-f74b-546b-b87e-a22ca804ac3f" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473954} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a89bbf83-2e3e-5555-a6d5-981a9278f764" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473120} {:answer/id #uuid "cea56d01-fdfe-5736-816e-b8204e960080" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473121}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a89bbf83-2e3e-5555-a6d5-981a9278f764" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473120} :answer-field/id #uuid "8372ee30-4548-5d83-9957-bf0d65799b1f" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473955} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc580dff-bc2e-5878-b7a7-f48a863b4636" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473122} {:answer/id #uuid "2be2d645-5052-599b-a84f-9d2d9883a16a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2be2d645-5052-599b-a84f-9d2d9883a16a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473123} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d08e1cd-2808-5a00-b091-ce22e53c0263" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473956}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "72e836b6-2968-5b2e-8666-6c15080ad3e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-42005" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 9 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{32}\\ne 0$ (condition  II is violated). \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since ${b}_{21}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 9 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is in row echelon form."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Matrices in Row Echelon Form"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129176 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128995 :question/id #uuid "7fd5c01f-c20e-5c47-b8d9-8cfbe634c14d" :question/math-academy-id "e-6166" :question/problem "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n![](images/85/8579b0afd584298a247c38af153d4e69945e73923e9605a168734c9250f3d18a.svg)" :question/worked-solution "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th rows of $A$ are $-1$, $-4$ and $8$, respectively.\n\n![](images/11/11af9a5354d23586af399f9bfade0641e9bb10898068ea825755de5c645e3d9c.svg)\n\nSo, the answer is $-1+(-4)+8=3.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "31c3678b-4f00-54d6-bb84-c7718fd622cb" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050163 :topic/math-academy-id 1167 :topic/title "Index Notation for Matrices"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129776 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5da3307-45b7-5e9f-a6a9-658f6827340b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128138} {:answer/id #uuid "bc8cbdc7-7567-56cc-8d55-dc3c4c7b565a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128139} {:answer/id #uuid "dbdcaeb0-9527-5770-8701-cba329b9819b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128140} {:answer/id #uuid "e296c04e-9507-5a04-b94f-9d47fdb50e15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128141} {:answer/id #uuid "33bc9a7c-58bf-52ef-9a75-10ceecc3d143" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128142}] :answer-field/id #uuid "7befadfa-ae8b-5031-b843-c2f8edff91b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128137}] :question/id #uuid "a2cf9f95-71df-5204-ad8a-59de853d764f" :question/math-academy-id "q-42362" :question/problem "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th rows in the matrix $A$, given below?\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129777 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93adc8f4-4ed3-5fa8-868c-0f2a9799cda4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128144} {:answer/id #uuid "bc2e8202-0303-5b4b-9dc0-6e1d26fda482" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128145} {:answer/id #uuid "0947f161-c